Source: lys-shell
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 desktop-file-utils
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys-shell
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys-shell.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys-shell

Package: lys-shell
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 hicolor-icon-theme,
 libpam0g
Recommends:
 libvulkan1,
 mesa-vulkan-drivers,
 xdg-desktop-portal
Suggests:
 dbus-user-session,
 bluez,
 network-manager,
 upower,
 power-profiles-daemon,
 pipewire-pulse,
 wireplumber
Description: Wayland desktop shell
 lys-shell is a compositor-agnostic Wayland desktop shell: bar, dropdowns,
 launcher, notifications, OSD, lock screen, greeter and an xdg-desktop-portal
 backend, configured in YAML or through the lys-settings GUI.
 .
 The binaries are Go with no cgo; they load PAM at runtime, and Vulkan when
 it is installed (the screen recorder needs it, with a GPU that
 encodes H.264).
